TI  - Orbit-Attitude Cooperative Control for Micro-Nano Satellites with Input Saturation: Fault-tolerant Control Based on RBF Neural Network
T2  - 2023 35TH CHINESE CONTROL AND DECISION CONFERENCE, CCDC
CP  - 35th Chinese Control and Decision Conference (CCDC)
AB  - This paper investigates the fault-tolerant control (FTC) problem of the micro-nano satellite cluster (MNSC) orbit-attitude cooperative control system. The nonlinear orbit-attitude control system model for MNSC with actuator faults and input saturation is given, which represents the dynamic characteristics of satellites. The proposed control approach deals with bias fault and partial loss of effectiveness. A novel adaptive dynamic surface controller is designed based on a radial basis function (RBF) neural network, which is utilized to approximate the coupling torque of the orbital transfer and unknown disturbances in the space environment and guarantees the asymptotic output tracking and ultimate uniform boundedness of the closed-loop attitude control systems of MNSC when an actuator failure occurs. Next, a distributed observer is established for the leader-followers system whose system matrix is not known exactly and not all followers can obtain the dynamic characteristics of the virtual leader. Furthermore, the closed-loop system is proved to be ultimately uniformly bounded based on the Lyapunov stability theory. Finally, simulation results verify the effectiveness of the presented control strategy.
