TI  - Mechanical Vibrations on a Deployable Nanosatellite Antenna: SAR Performance Analysis
T2  - 2024 18TH EUROPEAN CONFERENCE ON ANTENNAS AND PROPAGATION, EUCAP
CP  - 18th European Conference on Antennas and Propagation (EuCAP)
AB  - The mechanical vibrations of a high-strain glassfibre composite deployable X-band synthetic aperture radar (SAR) antenna structure are investigated using a finite element method. The antenna is approximately 2 m x 0.3 m, and exhibits natural frequencies at 2.8 Hz and 7.6 Hz. The radiation patterns for a reflectarray formed from the structure are calculated using a ray-tracing approach for the nominal and mechanically deformed cases. The mechanically deformed antenna pattern is defocused, and a SAR system model shows this reduces the signal-to-noise ratio of a point scattering target by approximately 6 dB.
